# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files since the 
#   project is likely to be intended to be used with multiple versions of 
#   python. For an application, you should keep them in the repo.
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#1191, it is recommended to not commit 
#   Pipfile.lock to library projects. For an application projects, 
#   it is recommended to do so.
# Pipfile.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipenv, poetry.lock contains the exact version of each 
#   dependency installed and should be committed to version control.
# poetry.lock

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipenv, pdm.lock contains the exact version of each 
#   dependency installed and should be committed to version control.
# pdm.lock

